    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0535" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1001</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-07T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 7, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received December 9, 10.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2185. For Harrison from Anderson:</p>
                <p>8. Leaving to-night for Vienna. Safe-conduct granted to me for the round trip
                    although Austrian Legation had cognizance of President Wilson’s message and final resolution.</p>
                <p>In view Wilson’s telegram 2124, November
                    26, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d383-f1"/> suggest you enquire of Garrett in The Hague his views concerning
                        Károlyi’s reliability.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
